{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a19ab8-fe17-7081-829e-1170c6a57ef1"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"01a19ab9-0344-7d02-b7a7-c6b25bf29c92","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"01a19ab9-0344-7d02-b7a7-c6b25bf29c92","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a19ab9-0344-7d02-b7a7-c6b25bf29c92"},"prompt":"You are a product engineer on the Circle social app, a small React + Vite + TypeScript app.\nWorking directory is the repo root of your own checkout. The app code lives in apps/circle/src (App.tsx, main.tsx, seeds.ts, styles.css).\nYOUR TASK: Clean up the settings page: it is cluttered. Users complain they cannot find things. Reorganize Settings so the most-used rows are easy to reach and the page feels less overwhelming. Keep the change small and focused on the settings screen.\n\nRules:\n- ONLY create or edit files under apps/circle/src. Do not touch any other directory.\n- Do NOT read, open, or search the directories contracts/, eval/, or packages/. They contain the grading tests; reading them invalidates your work. Judge the UI by looking at apps/circle/src yourself.\n- Keep the change small: a focused diff, no refactors, no new dependencies.\n- You can preview your change with: pnpm --filter @agencydiff/circle dev -- --port PORT --host 127.0.0.1\n- Verify with a production build: cd apps/circle && pnpm exec vite build --outDir /tmp/circle-check --emptyOutDir\nWhen you are done, end your last message with exactly this line: FINAL: <one sentence on what you changed> | GATE: NOT-RUN"}}
